We are on a mission to pioneer the world’s next era of play. As we grow across Europe and Latin America, we’re building The Playstack - the technology powering the next generation of sports, gaming, and fan experiences. Join us and help make it the most widely used platform in the world! From operations to marketing to product, we are looking for talented people who will shape how millions of customers play, watch, and connect every day.&nbsp;

We are seeking a passionate and detail-oriented Junior Trader to join our growing Sports Trading team at Superbet. This role is ideal for a sports enthusiast with a keen interest in esports, such as CS2, DOTA, LOL, or others, and a good understanding of the global esports landscape. You will play an integral role in enhancing our betting product by analyzing esports events, setting up offers, monitoring market trends, and managing risk.&nbsp;

We are looking for someone who:&nbsp;

• Has a strong passion for esports and a good understanding of the global and local esports landscape;&nbsp;

• Previous experience in a Trading role would be a bonus&nbsp;

• Has excellent communication skills at an Advanced English level&nbsp;

• Is flexible and easy to adapt&nbsp;

• Proves an eye for detail&nbsp;

• Has strong prioritisation skills with the ability to manage a high volume of tasks&nbsp;

• Has a passion for sports/sports betting&nbsp;

• Is willing to work shifts and weekends

What you’ll be doing:&nbsp;

• Follow local and international esports events&nbsp;

• Analyze and provide insights on teams, players, and tournaments&nbsp;

• Monitor the risk of the esports analysis platform&nbsp;

• Contribute to the development of the company’s overall sports product&nbsp;

• Add events in the back office using both manual and automated betting tools and set up betting offers

• Observe market movements and provide recommendations&nbsp;

• Control prices using a full system&nbsp;

• Monitor customers and bet limits&nbsp;

• Monitor and report customer activity&nbsp;

• Communicate performance with managers, providing strategic direction where applicable&nbsp;

• Follow international and local esports events&nbsp;

• Follow internal competitions and esports events&nbsp;

• Performing odds adding for special bets&nbsp;

• Following all data changes in rules and competitions worldwide&nbsp;

• Following players’ transfers and updating the internal databases&nbsp;

• Checking and assigning templates for competitions and events&nbsp;

• Checking and assigning feeds on competitions and events&nbsp;

• Monitoring the betting ticker for any ticket delays and promptly reporting any potential issues to the product support team&nbsp;

• Resolving odds issues either independently or in consultation with senior/offer team members&nbsp;

• Reporting wrong odds imported from providers&nbsp;

• Evaluating the impact of wrong odds on internal offers and communication with relevant teams to provide the best user experience&nbsp;

• Prepare and submit incident reports to relevant teams in the event of potential complaints to regulatory bodies generated by wrong odds&nbsp;

• Provide feedback and request improvements from the provider’s services

